  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1)\nToday looks to be the coolest day of the week as temperatures trend \nabove seasonal normals the rest of the week and weekend.\n\nSurface high pressure drifts to our southeast tonight, allowing for\nreturn flow to develop across the Ohio Valley. This southwesterly\nflow regime will usher in a warmer air mass on Wednesday, allowing\nhigh temps- to climb into the upper 70s to lower 80s. \n\nA weak cold front does appear to move through on Thursday, but not\nexpecting any pcpn with this passage. The main impact will be\ntemperatures dipping closer to normal values on Friday before quickly\nrebounding again on Saturday. Saturday is likely the warmest day of \nthe week, with most locations reaching the lower to middle 80s. \n\nThe main feature to monitor for the second half of the weekend will\nbe the track of tropical remnants from the Gulf. Several global\nmodels and ensembles do show this low tracking up into our CWA, which\nwould bring widespread precip to our fa Sunday if this track remains.\nWill continue to monitor forecast trends before diving into the \ndetails.",
